ces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049392 #edb/ref 1033 1023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049392 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "f1031f6b-01e9-5ea8-af71-27bacc9d53b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050463 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050463 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050463 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050463 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050463 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050463 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050463 #edb/ref 1031 "Representing 2x2 Systems of Equations Using a Matrix Product" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050463 #edb/ref 1033 1729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050463 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "4bb17014-060c-5398-ac8a-30c6798d15e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050656 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050656 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050656 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050656 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050656 #edb/ref 1031 "The Column Space of a Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050656 #edb/ref 1033 1850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050656 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5ce2b050-dd59-54b3-bb85-3a4f08ea0365" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186100866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186100867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186100868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1031 "Multiplying a Matrix by a Column Vector" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1033 1195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050825 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "69b57f07-ad86-5963-8f81-f63cb01f239f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059566 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4518" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059566 #edb/ref 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](images/ed/ed434344208758284aa0f144676f7dd6498a63faeb0248d18e87c4be6c3d87f2.png)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059566 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7bfcfcbb-6212-5f9b-90aa-c79fbf7221e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059566 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/b9/b9364923447e278db5ec47bef74e1a05310645b30df22d4ea5efcc0de46c6ed2.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/16/16cb1608f70821d138f0c6984038bb42d86d9fbf76d560d94d2e25bd6fdb05e0.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/0a/0abbbaf34955fa40d6cdbfa9e16cb1567ee16271d65b4565206a0f2204eedf6d.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/4b/4b915439c3e9922d692aab4205a728160e0a1286f82fa5ebc736460901581147.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059567 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4519" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059567 #edb/ref 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](images/c9/c9b7abb2641034c1769c6fe6b13b96edd7ccc282b61424b2031a3d37faa456e4.png)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059567 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c4af8b0d-e4ee-56f4-9cf6-594530639339" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059567 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](images/6f/6f1bf319faf8be4a9a79c0a6f9301e6eac48a5b04f66949b679e8445b07e9d9c.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](images/fc/fc1ac06787ed64ebefbb1a7a82f9bf785525777f61831bbbc39bd25c7e629d5a.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](images/d0/d0249dcecf6b75cd6ff7c4623beac6fd6cfae64a58d043bb6759440167f40ea1.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](images/64/64d1f57717dda57c8a7fbc403728ee9699a22ce995f68a50a0b80f25543fdab6.png)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186059566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059757 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186059953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186265931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186345101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186360768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186059567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059758 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059888 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059888 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059888 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186060664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059888 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059888 #edb/ref 1045 "Representing 3x3 Systems of Equations Using a Matrix Product" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059888 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186060662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059888 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059888 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "57e9a8cd-9225-5fac-965e-807daa0874c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060276 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060276 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36181" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060276 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060276 #edb/ref 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y+z=2 \\\\ x-6y+11z=3 \\\\ 3x-4y-z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & a \\\\ 1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060276 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5006a5f1-0a5e-50bb-a47b-7da41b1e709f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060276 #edb/ref 1074 "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=11.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060662 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060662 #edb/ref 1061 16480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060662 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "944c9195-2d49-5b9d-bc5c-1cd47e01dc13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060662 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060663 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060663 #edb/ref 1061 16482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060663 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c9335040-4892-53be-90b2-54e91913879f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060663 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060664 #edb/ref 1061 16483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060664 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "02ca150a-020c-573f-96d1-90c2f5331c52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060664 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060935 #edb/ref 1064 "Remember that we can represent a system of two linear equations in two variables using matrices. We can do the same thing for a system of three linear equations in three variables, such as the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y\\text{ }-\\text{ }2z=7 \\\\ 2x\\text{ }-\\text{ }1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }4z=2 \\\\ 2x+1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a $3 \\times 3$ system like the one above, we put the coefficients of the system into a $3 \\times 3$ coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nEach row has the coefficients of one of the equations in the system, and each column consists of the coefficients of one particular variable.\nWe also have the $3 \\times 1$ column vectors\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{b}$ consists of each constant on the right side of the system and $\\mathbf{x}$ contains the variables.\nWith these matrices, we can write our system as $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ or\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe can write any system of three equations with three variables in this form. Just to check that the above equation is true, let's multiply out the left-hand side to see if it equals the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3x+2y\\text{ }-\\text{ }2z \\\\ 2x\\text{ }-\\text{ }1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }4z \\\\ 2x+1y\\text{ }-\\text{ }3z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =b\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060935 #edb/ref 1065 3053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060935 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "93427b42-9f68-58e3-a3fd-19c5c8c58d90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186060935 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263842 #edb/ref 1080 "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263842 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263842 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "61b6213e-6630-5cbc-a2be-bba26537e9d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264311 #edb/ref 1080 "a=-4,\\,b=8,\\,c=-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264311 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264311 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "98683e89-44c4-5b63-a6a0-5143070e1a4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264374 #edb/ref 1080 "a=0,\\,b=8,\\,c=1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264374 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264374 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a16f2ca2-4f2e-5acc-9b55-06d4bbfa6420" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264916 #edb/ref 1080 "a=1,\\,b=7,\\,c=8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264916 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264916 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dc08dfd2-1ae1-53cb-adad-40873d7ac878" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265185 #edb/ref 1080 "a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265185 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265185 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f9db3e03-47ba-53e0-8851-1e7f8c0aa7b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265304 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186263842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265304 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265304 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265304 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186264916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265304 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186265185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265304 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265304 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265304 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186265185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265304 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "21ecd5d5-730f-53a8-b7fd-5892a28e6ac7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265930 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186265304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265930 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130536" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265930 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265930 #edb/ref 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ -6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265930 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "718180b1-bf73-575f-add7-0f6c8d9bba0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265930 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297603 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297603 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297603 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "09ca9278-0c20-567c-a5f8-c1e5fc82c7b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297639 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297639 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297639 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "146371ee-1c0b-5294-90fc-369dd2c1ae84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297828 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297828 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297828 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "43fddea3-d0f8-5695-aeca-4914b81fc7dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297949 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297949 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186297949 #edb/r